Objective

Answer "What will happen?" — predict whether a shipment will be delayed, 
and if so, estimate how long the delay will be. 
This feeds directly into Module 3's optimization engine.

Module2_Part1_Data_Preprocessing.ipynb
Commit message: Add data preprocessing — load Module 1 data, sanity checks, encoding pipeline
Description: Loads the train/test data and both targets from Module 1, 
checks for missing values and target balance, and builds 
a leakage-safe preprocessing pipeline (frequency encoding for high-cardinality columns, 
one-hot encoding for the rest). 

Module2_Part2_Classification_Model.ipynb
Commit message: Add classification model — predict late_delivery_risk (XGBoost vs LightGBM)
Description: Trains and compares XGBoost and LightGBM classifiers to predict whether 
a shipment will be delayed. Evaluates with accuracy, precision, recall, F1, ROC-AUC, 
confusion matrix, feature importance, and 5-fold cross-validation. 
Saves the best model (XGBoost, ROC-AUC 0.849).


Module2_Part3_Regression_Model.ipynb
Commit message: Add regression model — predict delay_duration_days (XGBoost vs LightGBM)
Description: Trains and compares XGBoost and LightGBM regressors to predict expected delay 
length in days. Evaluates with MAE, RMSE, R², predicted-vs-actual plots, feature importance, 
and 5-fold cross-validation. Saves the best model (XGBoost, MAE 0.663).

Module2_Part4_Module3_Handoff.ipynb
Commit message: Add Module 3 handoff — combine predictions into module3_input_predictions.csv
Description: Loads both trained models, reproduces the preprocessing pipeline on the test set, 
generates delay probability and expected delay duration for every shipment, and combines 
these with cost/timing/business columns into the file Module 3 needs for its optimization engine.
